{"id":"mahabharata-12-136","work":"mahabharata","part":12,"partName":"शान्तिपर्व","partNameEn":"Shanti Parva","unit":136,"title":"षट्त्रिंशदधिकशततमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 136 · The cat and the mouse","summary":{"en":"Yudhishthira asks how a man is to act when two strong foes threaten him, and Bhishma tells the tale of a cat caught in a net and the mouse who made friends with him. The two help each other to survive, and the lesson is when to trust an enemy for a common good and when to part from him.","kn":"ಇಬ್ಬರು ಬಲಿಷ್ಠ ಶತ್ರುಗಳು ಬೆದರಿಸಿದಾಗ ಹೇಗೆ ನಡೆಯಬೇಕೆಂದು ಯುಧಿಷ್ಠಿರ ಕೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ; ಬಲೆಯಲ್ಲಿ ಸಿಕ್ಕಿದ ಬೆಕ್ಕು ಮತ್ತು ಅದರೊಡನೆ ಸ್ನೇಹ ಬೆಳೆಸಿದ ಇಲಿಯ ಕಥೆಯನ್ನು ಭೀಷ್ಮ ಹೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ. ಇಬ್ಬರೂ ಪರಸ್ಪರ ಸಹಾಯದಿಂದ ಬದುಕುತ್ತಾರೆ; ಸಾಮಾನ್ಯ ಒಳಿತಿಗಾಗಿ ಶತ್ರುವನ್ನು ಯಾವಾಗ ನಂಬಬೇಕು, ಯಾವಾಗ ಬಿಡಬೇಕೆಂಬುದು ಪಾಠ.","hi":"युधिष्ठिर पूछते हैं कि दो बलवान शत्रुओं के धमकाने पर कैसे चलें, और भीष्म जाल में फँसे बिल्ले और उससे मित्रता करने वाले चूहे की कथा कहते हैं। दोनों एक-दूसरे की सहायता से बचते हैं, और सीख है कि साझे हित में शत्रु पर कब भरोसा करें और कब अलग हों।","te":"ఇద్దరు బలవంతులైన శత్రువులు బెదిరించినప్పుడు ఎలా నడుచుకోవాలని యుధిష్ఠిరుడు అడుగుతాడు; వలలో చిక్కిన పిల్లి, దానితో స్నేహం చేసిన ఎలుక కథను భీష్ముడు చెబుతాడు. ఇద్దరు ఒకరి సహాయంతో ఒకరు బతుకుతారు; ఉమ్మడి మేలు కోసం శత్రువును ఎప్పుడు నమ్మాలి, ఎప్పుడు వదలాలనేది పాఠం.","ta":"இரு வலிய பகைவர் அச்சுறுத்தும்போது எவ்வாறு நடப்பது என்று யுதிஷ்டிரர் கேட்க, வலையில் சிக்கிய பூனையும் அதனுடன் நட்பு கொண்ட எலியும் பற்றிய கதையைப் பீஷ்மர் கூறுகிறார். இருவரும் ஒருவருக்கு ஒருவர் உதவி பிழைக்கின்றனர்; பொது நன்மைக்காகப் பகைவனை எப்போது நம்புவது, எப்போது பிரிவது என்பது பாடம்.","ml":"ശക്തരായ രണ്ടു ശത്രുക്കൾ ഭീഷണിപ്പെടുത്തുമ്പോൾ മനുഷ്യൻ എങ്ങനെ പ്രവർത്തിക്കണമെന്ന് യുധിഷ്ഠിരൻ ചോദിക്കുന്നു; വലയിൽ കുടുങ്ങിയ പൂച്ചയുടെയും അവനുമായി സൗഹൃദമുണ്ടാക്കിയ എലിയുടെയും കഥ ഭീഷ്മർ പറയുന്നു. ഇരുവരും പരസ്പരം സഹായിച്ച് രക്ഷപ്പെടുന്നു; പൊതുനന്മയ്ക്കായി ശത്രുവിനെ എപ്പോൾ വിശ്വസിക്കണമെന്നും എപ്പോൾ പിരിയണമെന്നും ഇതിൽനിന്ന് പഠിക്കാമെന്ന് അദ്ദേഹം പറയുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 12.136; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Wed Jun 16 2021","sections":[{"title":"आपद्धर्मपर्व","titleEn":"Apaddharma Parva (Duties in distress)","verses":[{"text":"युधिष्ठिर उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Yudhishthira said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"सर्वत्र बुद्धिः कथिता श्रेष्ठा ते भरतर्षभ ।\nअनागता तथोत्पन्ना दीर्घसूत्रा विनाशिनी ॥","meaning":{"en":"Best of the Bharatas, you have said that intelligence is best everywhere, and that the procrastinator who lets things drag is destroyed, whether the trouble has not yet come or has already arisen."}},{"n":2,"text":"तदिच्छामि परां बुद्धिं श्रोतुं भरतसत्तम ।\nयथा राजन्न मुह्येत शत्रुभिः परिवारितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"I wish to hear of that supreme intelligence, best of the Bharatas, by which a king surrounded by enemies is not bewildered."}},{"n":3,"text":"धर्मार्थकुशल प्राज्ञ सर्वशास्त्रविशारद ।\nपृच्छामि त्वा कुरुश्रेष्ठ तन्मे व्याख्यातुमर्हसि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Wise one, skilled in dharma and wealth and learned in all the scriptures, best of the Kurus, I ask you; you should explain it to me."}},{"n":4,"text":"शत्रुभिर्बहुभिर्ग्रस्तो यथा वर्तेत पार्थिवः ।\nएतदिच्छाम्यहं श्रोतुं सर्वमेव यथाविधि ॥","meaning":{"en":"I wish to hear fully and properly how a king should act when beset by many enemies."}},{"n":5,"text":"विषमस्थं हि राजानं शत्रवः परिपन्थिनः ।\nबहवोऽप्येकमुद्धर्तुं यतन्ते पूर्वतापिताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"For when a king is in a bad position, hostile enemies, though many, strive to lift him out, having been harassed by him before."}},{"n":6,"text":"सर्वतः प्रार्थ्यमानेन दुर्बलेन महाबलैः ।\nएकेनैवासहायेन शक्यं स्थातुं कथं भवेत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"How can one weak and alone, without allies, sought on all sides by great powers, manage to hold his ground?"}},{"n":7,"text":"कथं मित्रमरिं चैव विन्देत भरतर्षभ ।\nचेष्टितव्यं कथं चात्र शत्रोर्मित्रस्य चान्तरे ॥","meaning":{"en":"How, best of the Bharatas, is one to find a friend or an enemy, and how should one act here between enemy and friend?"}},{"n":8,"text":"प्रज्ञातलक्षणे राजन्नमित्रे मित्रतां गते ।\nकथं नु पुरुषः कुर्यात्किं वा कृत्वा सुखी भवेत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"When an enemy of known marks has turned friend, king, what should a man do, or what doing would make him happy?"}},{"n":9,"text":"विग्रहं केन वा कुर्यात्संधिं वा केन योजयेत् ।\nकथं वा शत्रुमध्यस्थो वर्तेताबलवानिति ॥","meaning":{"en":"With whom should he wage war, with whom should he join in peace, and how should a weak man behave in the midst of enemies?"}},{"n":10,"text":"एतद्वै सर्वकृत्यानां परं कृत्यं परंतप ।\nनैतस्य कश्चिद्वक्तास्ति श्रोता चापि सुदुर्लभः ॥","meaning":{"en":"This, scorcher of foes, is the highest of all duties; there is no one who can tell it, and a listener is very hard to find,"}},{"n":11,"text":"ऋते शांतनवाद्भीष्मात्सत्यसंधाज्जितेन्द्रियात् ।\nतदन्विष्य महाबाहो सर्वमेतद्वदस्व मे ॥","meaning":{"en":"except Bhishma, son of Shantanu, true to his promise and master of his senses. Seek it out, mighty-armed one, and tell me all this."}},{"text":"भीष्म उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Bhishma said:"}},{"n":12,"text":"त्वद्युक्तोऽयमनुप्रश्नो युधिष्ठिर गुणोदयः ।\nशृणु मे पुत्र कार्त्स्न्येन गुह्यमापत्सु भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Yudhishthira, this question of yours is fitting and shows excellent qualities. Hear from me fully, my son, Bharata, the secret for times of calamity."}},{"n":13,"text":"अमित्रो मित्रतां याति मित्रं चापि प्रदुष्यति ।\nसामर्थ्ययोगात्कार्याणां तद्गत्या हि सदा गतिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"An enemy becomes a friend and a friend turns bad, by the pressure of affairs and by power; for movement always follows the movement of circumstances."}},{"n":14,"text":"तस्माद्विश्वसितव्यं च विग्रहं च समाचरेत् ।\nदेशं कालं च विज्ञाय कार्याकार्यविनिश्चये ॥","meaning":{"en":"Therefore one should trust, and also make war, after judging place and time and deciding what should and should not be done."}},{"n":15,"text":"संधातव्यं बुधैर्नित्यं व्यवस्यं च हितार्थिभिः ।\nअमित्रैरपि संधेयं प्राणा रक्ष्याश्च भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"The wise should always make alliances and those who seek their welfare should resolve to do so; one should make peace even with enemies, Bharata, and protect one's life."}},{"n":16,"text":"यो ह्यमित्रैर्नरो नित्यं न संदध्यादपण्डितः ।\nन सोऽर्थमाप्नुयात्किंचित्फलान्यपि च भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"The unwise man who never makes terms with enemies will gain no wealth and not even results, Bharata."}},{"n":17,"text":"यस्त्वमित्रेण संधत्ते मित्रेण च विरुध्यते ।\nअर्थयुक्तिं समालोक्य सुमहद्विन्दते फलम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"But one who allies with an enemy and quarrels with a friend, judging the connection of aims, gains a very great result."}},{"n":18,"text":"अत्राप्युदाहरन्तीममितिहासं पुरातनम् ।\nमार्जारस्य च संवादं न्यग्रोधे मूषकस्य च ॥","meaning":{"en":"On this they also recount an ancient tale, the conversation between a cat and a mouse in a banyan tree."}},{"n":19,"text":"वने महति कस्मिंश्चिन्न्यग्रोधः सुमहानभूत् ।\nलताजालपरिच्छन्नो नानाद्विजगणायुतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"In a certain great forest there stood a huge banyan, covered with a net of creepers and filled with flocks of many birds."}},{"n":20,"text":"स्कन्धवान्मेघसंकाशः शीतच्छायो मनोरमः ।\nवैरन्त्यमभितो जातस्तरुर्व्यालमृगाकुलः ॥","meaning":{"en":"It had a great trunk, like a cloud, with cool shade, delightful, grown at the edge of a border land and teeming with beasts of prey."}},{"n":21,"text":"तस्य मूलं समाश्रित्य कृत्वा शतमुखं बिलम् ।\nवसति स्म महाप्राज्ञः पलितो नाम मूषकः ॥","meaning":{"en":"A very wise mouse named Palita lived at its root, having made a burrow with a hundred openings."}},{"n":22,"text":"शाखाश्च तस्य संश्रित्य वसति स्म सुखं पुरः ।\nलोमशो नाम मार्जारः पक्षिसत्त्वावसादकः ॥","meaning":{"en":"And a cat named Lomasha, destroyer of birds and animals, lived happily in its branches."}},{"n":23,"text":"तत्र चागत्य चण्डालो वैरन्त्यकृतकेतनः ।\nअयोजयत्तमुन्माथं नित्यमस्तं गते रवौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"A Chandala who lived at the border came there and each day at sunset set a snare."}},{"n":24,"text":"तत्र स्नायुमयान्पाशान्यथावत्संनिधाय सः ।\nगृहं गत्वा सुखं शेते प्रभातामेति शर्वरीम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having duly laid sinew snares there, he went home, slept happily, and came back when the night was over."}},{"n":25,"text":"तत्र स्म नित्यं बध्यन्ते नक्तं बहुविधा मृगाः ।\nकदाचित्तत्र मार्जारस्त्वप्रमत्तोऽप्यबध्यत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Every night many kinds of animals were caught there. Once, the cat, though careful, was caught."}},{"n":26,"text":"तस्मिन्बद्धे महाप्राज्ञः शत्रौ नित्याततायिनि ।\nतं कालं पलितो ज्ञात्वा विचचार सुनिर्भयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"When that enemy, ever ready to strike, was caught, the very wise Palita, knowing the time, roamed about quite fearlessly."}},{"n":27,"text":"तेनानुचरता तस्मिन्वने विश्वस्तचारिणा ।\nभक्षं विचरमाणेन नचिराद्दृष्टमामिषम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Roaming trustingly in that forest in search of food, he soon spotted some meat."}},{"n":28,"text":"स तमुन्माथमारुह्य तदामिषमभक्षयत् ।\nतस्योपरि सपत्नस्य बद्धस्य मनसा हसन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Climbing onto that snare, he ate the meat, laughing in his mind at his enemy who lay caught beneath him."}},{"n":29,"text":"आमिषे तु प्रसक्तः स कदाचिदवलोकयन् ।\nअपश्यदपरं घोरमात्मनः शत्रुमागतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Once, absorbed in the meat, as he looked about he saw another dreadful enemy of his arriving."}},{"n":30,"text":"शरप्रसूनसंकाशं महीविवरशायिनम् ।\nनकुलं हरिकं नाम चपलं ताम्रलोचनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"It was a mongoose named Harika, the color of a reed flower, living in a hole in the ground, restless, with copper-red eyes."}},{"n":31,"text":"तेन मूषकगन्धेन त्वरमाणमुपागतम् ।\nभक्षार्थं लेलिहद्वक्त्रं भूमावूर्ध्वमुखं स्थितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Drawn by the mouse's scent, it came hurrying, licking its mouth, and stood on the ground face upward, for food."}},{"n":32,"text":"शाखागतमरिं चान्यदपश्यत्कोटरालयम् ।\nउलूकं चन्द्रकं नाम तीक्ष्णतुण्डं क्षपाचरम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"He also saw another enemy on a branch, living in a hollow: an owl named Chandraka, sharp-beaked, a night-roamer."}},{"n":33,"text":"गतस्य विषयं तस्य नकुलोलूकयोस्तदा ।\nअथास्यासीदियं चिन्ता तत्प्राप्य सुमहद्भयम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"When the mongoose and owl had come within range, this worry came to him, and he felt great fear."}},{"n":34,"text":"आपद्यस्यां सुकष्टायां मरणे समुपस्थिते ।\nसमन्ताद्भय उत्पन्ने कथं कार्यं हितैषिणा ॥","meaning":{"en":"In this very painful calamity, with death at hand and fear arising on all sides, what should one wishing for his own good do?"}},{"n":35,"text":"स तथा सर्वतो रुद्धः सर्वत्र समदर्शनः ।\nअभवद्भयसंतप्तश्चक्रे चेमां परां गतिम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Thus blocked on all sides, looking everywhere equally, he was scorched with fear and reached this best resolve."}},{"n":36,"text":"आपद्विनाशभूयिष्ठा शतैकीयं च जीवितम् ।\nसमन्तसंशया चेयमस्मानापदुपस्थिता ॥","meaning":{"en":"'Calamity is mostly destruction, and life depends on a hundredth part. Such a calamity, doubtful on every side, has come upon me."}},{"n":37,"text":"गतं हि सहसा भूमिं नकुलो मां समाप्नुयात् ।\nउलूकश्चेह तिष्ठन्तं मार्जारः पाशसंक्षयात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"If I go suddenly to the ground, the mongoose will get me; if I stay here, the owl will; and the cat would, once the snare is destroyed."}},{"n":38,"text":"न त्वेवास्मद्विधः प्राज्ञः संमोहं गन्तुमर्हति ।\nकरिष्ये जीविते यत्नं यावदुच्छ्वासनिग्रहम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"But a wise one like me should not fall into confusion. I will strive for life as long as I can hold my breath."}},{"n":39,"text":"न हि बुद्ध्यान्विताः प्राज्ञा नीतिशास्त्रविशारदाः ।\nसंभ्रमन्त्यापदं प्राप्य महतोऽर्थानवाप्य च ॥","meaning":{"en":"For the wise, endowed with intelligence and skilled in the science of policy, do not panic on reaching calamity, even when they have obtained great gains."}},{"n":40,"text":"न त्वन्यामिह मार्जाराद्गतिं पश्यामि सांप्रतम् ।\nविषमस्थो ह्ययं जन्तुः कृत्यं चास्य महन्मया ॥","meaning":{"en":"I see no other way now but through the cat. This creature is in a bad position, and I have a great task regarding him."}},{"n":41,"text":"जीवितार्थी कथं त्वद्य प्रार्थितः शत्रुभिस्त्रिभिः ।\nतस्मादिममहं शत्रुं मार्जारं संश्रयामि वै ॥","meaning":{"en":"How, wishing to live, can I now be sought by three enemies? So I will take refuge with this enemy, the cat."}},{"n":42,"text":"क्षत्रविद्यां समाश्रित्य हितमस्योपधारये ।\nयेनेमं शत्रुसंघातं मतिपूर्वेण वञ्चये ॥","meaning":{"en":"Relying on the science of warriors, I will think of his benefit, by which I may deliberately deceive this band of enemies."}},{"n":43,"text":"अयमत्यन्तशत्रुर्मे वैषम्यं परमं गतः ।\nमूढो ग्राहयितुं स्वार्थं संगत्या यदि शक्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"This extreme enemy of mine has fallen into the worst plight; if it is possible, by association, to make this fool take up his own interest,"}},{"n":44,"text":"कदाचिद्व्यसनं प्राप्य संधिं कुर्यान्मया सह ।\nबलिना संनिविष्टस्य शत्रोरपि परिग्रहः ।\nकार्य इत्याहुराचार्या विषमे जीवितार्थिना ॥","meaning":{"en":"perhaps in his misfortune he will make peace with me. The teachers say that even an enemy who has been put in a place by a strong one should be taken in by one wishing to live, in a bad position."}},{"n":45,"text":"श्रेयान्हि पण्डितः शत्रुर्न च मित्रमपण्डितम् ।\nमम ह्यमित्रे मार्जारे जीवितं संप्रतिष्ठितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"A wise enemy is better than an unwise friend; my life now depends on my enemy the cat."}},{"n":46,"text":"हन्तैनं संप्रवक्ष्यामि हेतुमात्माभिरक्षणे ।\nअपीदानीमयं शत्रुः संगत्या पण्डितो भवेत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Well then, I will give him a reason for protecting himself. Perhaps now, by association, this enemy may become wise.'"}},{"n":47,"text":"ततोऽर्थगतितत्त्वज्ञः संधिविग्रहकालवित् ।\nसान्त्वपूर्वमिदं वाक्यं मार्जारं मूषकोऽब्रवीत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the mouse, who knew the truth of the course of affairs and the time for peace and war, spoke these words to the cat, conciliating him first."}},{"n":48,"text":"सौहृदेनाभिभाषे त्वा कच्चिन्मार्जार जीवसि ।\nजीवितं हि तवेच्छामि श्रेयः साधारणं हि नौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"'I speak to you in friendship: cat, are you alive? I want you to live, for the good we both have is shared."}},{"n":49,"text":"न ते सौम्य विषत्तव्यं जीविष्यसि यथा पुरा ।\nअहं त्वामुद्धरिष्यामि प्राणाञ्जह्यां हि ते कृते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Gentle one, you need not despair; you will live as before. I will lift you out, and I would even give up my life for you."}},{"n":50,"text":"अस्ति कश्चिदुपायोऽत्र पुष्कलः प्रतिभाति माम् ।\nयेन शक्यस्त्वया मोक्षः प्राप्तुं श्रेयो यथा मया ॥","meaning":{"en":"A full means occurs to me here, by which you may be freed and gain good, as I will."}},{"n":51,"text":"मया ह्युपायो दृष्टोऽयं विचार्य मतिमात्मनः ।\nआत्मार्थं च त्वदर्थं च श्रेयः साधारणं हि नौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"I have seen this means by thinking it through with my own mind, for my own sake and yours; for the good we both have is shared."}},{"n":52,"text":"इदं हि नकुलोलूकं पापबुद्ध्यभितः स्थितम् ।\nन धर्षयति मार्जार तेन मे स्वस्ति सांप्रतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"This mongoose and this owl stand around me with evil intent, cat, and do not yet attack me; so I am well just now."}},{"n":53,"text":"कूजंश्चपलनेत्रोऽयं कौशिको मां निरीक्षते ।\nनगशाखाग्रहस्तिष्ठंस्तस्याहं भृशमुद्विजे ॥","meaning":{"en":"This owl, with restless eyes, hoots and looks at me. Perched at the tip of a branch, I am greatly alarmed at him."}},{"n":54,"text":"सतां साप्तपदं सख्यं सवासो मेऽसि पण्डितः ।\nसांवास्यकं करिष्यामि नास्ति ते मृत्युतो भयम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Friendship among the good arises in seven steps. You, being wise, are my dwelling companion; I will keep company with you, and you have no fear of death."}},{"n":55,"text":"न हि शक्नोषि मार्जार पाशं छेत्तुं विना मया ।\nअहं छेत्स्यामि ते पाशं यदि मां त्वं न हिंससि ॥","meaning":{"en":"You cannot cut the snare without me, cat. I will cut your snare if you do not harm me."}},{"n":56,"text":"त्वमाश्रितो नगस्याग्रं मूलं त्वहमुपाश्रितः ।\nचिरोषिताविहावां वै वृक्षेऽस्मिन्विदितं हि ते ॥","meaning":{"en":"You live at the top of the tree and I dwell at the root; we have lived here a long time, as you know."}},{"n":57,"text":"यस्मिन्नाश्वसते कश्चिद्यश्च नाश्वसते क्वचित् ।\nन तौ धीराः प्रशंसन्ति नित्यमुद्विग्नचेतसौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"One in whom no one trusts and one who trusts no one anywhere: the steady do not praise either, for they are always troubled in mind."}},{"n":58,"text":"तस्माद्विवर्धतां प्रीतिः सत्या संगतिरस्तु नौ ।\nकालातीतमपार्थं हि न प्रशंसन्ति पण्डिताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"So let our affection grow, and let our alliance be real; the wise do not praise what is out of time and pointless."}},{"n":59,"text":"अर्थयुक्तिमिमां तावद्यथाभूतां निशामय ।\nतव जीवितमिच्छामि त्वं ममेच्छसि जीवितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Now hear this connection of interests as it really is: I want your life and you want mine."}},{"n":60,"text":"कश्चित्तरति काष्ठेन सुगम्भीरां महानदीम् ।\nस तारयति तत्काष्ठं स च काष्ठेन तार्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"One man crosses a very deep great river by a log; he carries the log across, and he is carried across by the log."}},{"n":61,"text":"ईदृशो नौ समायोगो भविष्यति सुनिस्तरः ।\nअहं त्वां तारयिष्यामि त्वं च मां तारयिष्यसि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Such will be our alliance, easy to cross by: I will take you across and you will take me across.'"}},{"n":62,"text":"एवमुक्त्वा तु पलितस्तदर्थमुभयोर्हितम् ।\nहेतुमद्ग्रहणीयं च कालाकाङ्क्षी व्यपैक्षत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having thus spoken of their mutual benefit, Palita, awaiting the right moment, watched for the reasoned reply."}},{"n":63,"text":"अथ सुव्याहृतं तस्य श्रुत्वा शत्रुर्विचक्षणः ।\nहेतुमद्ग्रहणीयार्थं मार्जारो वाक्यमब्रवीत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the shrewd enemy, the cat, hearing his well-spoken words, answered with a reasoned remark that should be taken up."}},{"n":64,"text":"बुद्धिमान्वाक्यसंपन्नस्तद्वाक्यमनुवर्णयन् ।\nतामवस्थामवेक्ष्यान्त्यां साम्नैव प्रत्यपूजयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Intelligent and eloquent, he repeated his words, saw his final plight, and honored him with conciliatory speech alone."}},{"n":65,"text":"ततस्तीक्ष्णाग्रदशनो वैडूर्यमणिलोचनः ।\nमूषकं मन्दमुद्वीक्ष्य मार्जारो लोमशोऽब्रवीत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the cat Lomasha, with sharp-tipped teeth and eyes like cat's-eye gems, looked gently at the mouse and said:"}},{"n":66,"text":"नन्दामि सौम्य भद्रं ते यो मां जीवन्तमिच्छसि ।\nश्रेयश्च यदि जानीषे क्रियतां मा विचारय ॥","meaning":{"en":"'I am glad, gentle one; good fortune to you, since you want me to live. If you know what is best, do it; do not hesitate."}},{"n":67,"text":"अहं हि दृढमापन्नस्त्वमापन्नतरो मया ।\nद्वयोरापन्नयोः संधिः क्रियतां मा विचारय ॥","meaning":{"en":"I am deeply in trouble, but you are in more trouble than I; two in trouble should make peace; do not hesitate."}},{"n":68,"text":"विधत्स्व प्राप्तकालं यत्कार्यं सिध्यतु चावयोः ।\nमयि कृच्छ्राद्विनिर्मुक्ते न विनङ्क्ष्यति ते कृतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Do what the time requires, and let the task of both of us succeed. When I am freed from this hardship, what you have done will not be lost."}},{"n":69,"text":"न्यस्तमानोऽस्मि भक्तोऽस्मि शिष्यस्त्वद्धितकृत्तथा ।\nनिदेशवशवर्ती च भवन्तं शरणं गतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"I have cast away pride; I am devoted, a disciple doing your good, subject to your command, and I have come to you for refuge.'"}},{"n":70,"text":"इत्येवमुक्तः पलितो मार्जारं वशमागतम् ।\nवाक्यं हितमुवाचेदमभिनीतार्थमर्थवत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"So addressed, Palita, to the cat who had come under his power, spoke these beneficial and purposeful words, drawing out the matter."}},{"n":71,"text":"उदारं यद्भवानाह नैतच्चित्रं भवद्विधे ।\nविदितो यस्तु मार्गो मे हितार्थं शृणु तं मम ॥","meaning":{"en":"'What you say is noble, and it is no wonder in one like you. Hear the way I have found for our good."}},{"n":72,"text":"अहं त्वानुप्रवेक्ष्यामि नकुलान्मे महद्भयम् ।\nत्रायस्व मां मा वधीश्च शक्तोऽस्मि तव मोक्षणे ॥","meaning":{"en":"I will come in under you, for I have great fear of the mongoose. Protect me and do not kill me; I am able to free you."}},{"n":73,"text":"उलूकाच्चैव मां रक्ष क्षुद्रः प्रार्थयते हि माम् ।\nअहं छेत्स्यामि ते पाशान्सखे सत्येन ते शपे ॥","meaning":{"en":"And guard me from the owl too, for the little wretch seeks me. Friend, I will cut your snares; I swear it to you by truth.'"}},{"n":74,"text":"तद्वचः संगतं श्रुत्वा लोमशो युक्तमर्थवत् ।\nहर्षादुद्वीक्ष्य पलितं स्वागतेनाभ्यपूजयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hearing those apt, fitting and meaningful words, Lomasha looked at Palita with joy and welcomed him."}},{"n":75,"text":"स तं संपूज्य पलितं मार्जारः सौहृदे स्थितः ।\nसुविचिन्त्याब्रवीद्धीरः प्रीतस्त्वरित एव हि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having honored Palita, the cat, steady in friendship, thought it over well and, pleased and hurried, said:"}},{"n":76,"text":"क्षिप्रमागच्छ भद्रं ते त्वं मे प्राणसमः सखा ।\nतव प्राज्ञ प्रसादाद्धि क्षिप्रं प्राप्स्यामि जीवितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"'Come quickly, good fortune to you; you are a friend equal to my life. By your favor, wise one, I shall soon get my life."}},{"n":77,"text":"यद्यदेवंगतेनाद्य शक्यं कर्तुं मया तव ।\nतदाज्ञापय कर्ताहं संधिरेवास्तु नौ सखे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Whatever I can do for you today in such a plight, command it; I will do it, and let peace be between us, friend."}},{"n":78,"text":"अस्मात्ते संशयान्मुक्तः समित्रगणबान्धवः ।\nसर्वकार्याणि कर्ताहं प्रियाणि च हितानि च ॥","meaning":{"en":"Freed from this danger, with my circle of friends and kin, I will do all that is pleasing and beneficial."}},{"n":79,"text":"मुक्तश्च व्यसनादस्मात्सौम्याहमपि नाम ते ।\nप्रीतिमुत्पादयेयं च प्रतिकर्तुं च शक्नुयाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"And freed from this calamity, gentle one, I too may bring you joy and be able to repay you.'"}},{"n":80,"text":"ग्राहयित्वा तु तं स्वार्थं मार्जारं मूषकस्तदा ।\nप्रविवेश सुविस्रब्धः सम्यगर्थांश्चचार ह ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having made the cat take up his own interest, the mouse then went in with full trust and carried out things properly."}},{"n":81,"text":"एवमाश्वासितो विद्वान्मार्जारेण स मूषकः ।\nमार्जारोरसि विस्रब्धः सुष्वाप पितृमातृवत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Thus reassured by the cat, that learned mouse, trusting, slept on the cat's chest as on a father's or mother's."}},{"n":82,"text":"लीनं तु तस्य गात्रेषु मार्जारस्याथ मूषकम् ।\nतौ दृष्ट्वा नकुलोलूकौ निराशौ जग्मतुर्गृहान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing the mouse nestled in the cat's limbs, the mongoose and the owl lost hope and went home."}},{"n":83,"text":"लीनस्तु तस्य गात्रेषु पलितो देशकालवित् ।\nचिच्छेद पाशान्नृपते कालाकाङ्क्षी शनैः शनैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hidden in the cat's body, Palita, who knew place and time, waited for the moment and slowly, slowly cut the snares, O king."}},{"n":84,"text":"अथ बन्धपरिक्लिष्टो मार्जारो वीक्ष्य मूषकम् ।\nछिन्दन्तं वै तदा पाशानत्वरन्तं त्वरान्वितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the cat, distressed by his bonds, seeing the mouse cutting the snares unhurriedly, became impatient."}},{"n":85,"text":"तमत्वरन्तं पलितं पाशानां छेदने तदा ।\nसंचोदयितुमारेभे मार्जारो मूषकं तदा ॥","meaning":{"en":"As Palita did not hurry in cutting the snares, the cat then began to urge the mouse on."}},{"n":86,"text":"किं सौम्य नाभित्वरसे किं कृतार्थोऽवमन्यसे ।\nछिन्धि पाशानमित्रघ्न पुरा श्वपच एति सः ॥","meaning":{"en":"'Gentle one, why don't you hurry? Do you slight me now that your aim is gained? Cut the snares, slayer of enemies, before the dog-eater comes!'"}},{"n":87,"text":"इत्युक्तस्त्वरता तेन मतिमान्पलितोऽब्रवीत् ।\nमार्जारमकृतप्रज्ञं वश्यमात्महितं वचः ॥","meaning":{"en":"So urged in haste, the wise Palita spoke words to the heedless cat, now in his power, for his own good."}},{"n":88,"text":"तूष्णीं भव न ते सौम्य त्वरा कार्या न संभ्रमः ।\nवयमेवात्र कालज्ञा न कालः परिहास्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"'Be quiet, gentle one; you need not hurry or fuss. We ourselves know the time here; the time will not be lost."}},{"n":89,"text":"अकाले कृत्यमारब्धं कर्तुं नार्थाय कल्पते ।\nतदेव काल आरब्धं महतेऽर्थाय कल्पते ॥","meaning":{"en":"A task begun at the wrong time does not serve its purpose; the very same begun at the right time yields great gain."}},{"n":90,"text":"अकालविप्रमुक्तान्मे त्वत्त एव भयं भवेत् ।\nतस्मात्कालं प्रतीक्षस्व किमिति त्वरसे सखे ॥","meaning":{"en":"If I free you at the wrong time, the danger to me would be from you alone. So wait for the time; why do you hurry, friend?"}},{"n":91,"text":"यावत्पश्यामि चण्डालमायान्तं शस्त्रपाणिनम् ।\nततश्छेत्स्यामि ते पाशं प्राप्ते साधारणे भये ॥","meaning":{"en":"When I see the Chandala coming with a weapon in his hand, then I will cut your snare, when the danger is shared."}},{"n":92,"text":"तस्मिन्काले प्रमुक्तस्त्वं तरुमेवाधिरोहसि ।\nन हि ते जीवितादन्यत्किंचित्कृत्यं भविष्यति ॥","meaning":{"en":"At that time, freed, you will climb the tree itself; you will have no other task than your life."}},{"n":93,"text":"ततो भवत्यतिक्रान्ते त्रस्ते भीते च लोमश ।\nअहं बिलं प्रवेक्ष्यामि भवाञ्शाखां गमिष्यति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, Lomasha, when you are gone, terrified and frightened, I will enter my burrow and you will go to your branch.'"}},{"n":94,"text":"एवमुक्तस्तु मार्जारो मूषकेणात्मनो हितम् ।\nवचनं वाक्यतत्त्वज्ञो जीवितार्थी महामतिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"So addressed by the mouse, the cat, a clever man of words who wished to live, thought it was for his own good."}},{"n":95,"text":"अथात्मकृत्यत्वरितः सम्यक्प्रश्रयमाचरन् ।\nउवाच लोमशो वाक्यं मूषकं चिरकारिणम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, hurried for his own task and showing proper courtesy, Lomasha spoke to the slow mouse."}},{"n":96,"text":"न ह्येवं मित्रकार्याणि प्रीत्या कुर्वन्ति साधवः ।\nयथा त्वं मोक्षितः कृच्छ्रात्त्वरमाणेन वै मया ॥","meaning":{"en":"'Good people do not do for friends' tasks like this, with affection: you were freed from distress by me in a hurry,"}},{"n":97,"text":"तथैव त्वरमाणेन त्वया कार्यं हितं मम ।\nयत्नं कुरु महाप्राज्ञ यथा स्वस्त्यावयोर्भवेत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"so likewise you should do my benefit in haste. Strive, great sage, that we may both be safe."}},{"n":98,"text":"अथ वा पूर्ववैरं त्वं स्मरन्कालं विकर्षसि ।\nपश्य दुष्कृतकर्मत्वं व्यक्तमायुःक्षयो मम ॥","meaning":{"en":"Or are you, remembering our old enmity, dragging out the time? See how ill you act; clearly my life is ending."}},{"n":99,"text":"यच्च किंचिन्मयाज्ञानात्पुरस्ताद्विप्रियं कृतम् ।\nन तन्मनसि कर्तव्यं क्षमये त्वां प्रसीद मे ॥","meaning":{"en":"And whatever offense I did you in ignorance before, do not hold it in mind; I beg your pardon; be gracious to me.'"}},{"n":100,"text":"तमेवंवादिनं प्राज्ञः शास्त्रविद्बुद्धिसंमतः ।\nउवाचेदं वचः श्रेष्ठं मार्जारं मूषकस्तदा ॥","meaning":{"en":"To the cat speaking thus, the mouse, wise, learned and respected for his mind, then said this excellent word."}},{"n":101,"text":"श्रुतं मे तव मार्जार स्वमर्थं परिगृह्णतः ।\nममापि त्वं विजानीहि स्वमर्थं परिगृह्णतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"'I have heard you, cat, as you take up your own interest; know that I too am taking up mine."}},{"n":102,"text":"यन्मित्रं भीतवत्साध्यं यन्मित्रं भयसंहितम् ।\nसुरक्षितं ततः कार्यं पाणिः सर्पमुखादिव ॥","meaning":{"en":"A friend won over out of fear, a friend joined by fear, should be guarded well, like a hand near a snake's mouth."}},{"n":103,"text":"कृत्वा बलवता संधिमात्मानं यो न रक्षति ।\nअपथ्यमिव तद्भुक्तं तस्यानर्थाय कल्पते ॥","meaning":{"en":"One who, having made a pact with a strong one, does not protect himself, finds it turns to his harm, like unwholesome food eaten."}},{"n":104,"text":"न कश्चित्कस्यचिन्मित्रं न कश्चित्कस्यचित्सुहृत् ।\nअर्थैरर्था निबध्यन्ते गजैर्वनगजा इव ॥","meaning":{"en":"No one is anyone's friend and no one is anyone's well-wisher; interests are bound by interests, as wild elephants are bound by tame ones."}},{"n":105,"text":"न हि कश्चित्कृते कार्ये कर्तारं समवेक्षते ।\nतस्मात्सर्वाणि कार्याणि सावशेषाणि कारयेत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"When a task is done, no one looks to the doer; therefore one should do every task leaving something remaining."}},{"n":106,"text":"तस्मिन्कालेऽपि च भवान्दिवाकीर्तिभयान्वितः ।\nमम न ग्रहणे शक्तः पलायनपरायणः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Even at that time, you, fearful of the daylight-roaming Chandala, would be unable to seize me, intent on fleeing."}},{"n":107,"text":"छिन्नं तु तन्तुबाहुल्यं तन्तुरेकोऽवशेषितः ।\nछेत्स्याम्यहं तदप्याशु निर्वृतो भव लोमश ॥","meaning":{"en":"The great mass of threads is cut; one thread is left. I will cut that too quickly; be at ease, Lomasha."}},{"n":108,"text":"तयोः संवदतोरेवं तथैवापन्नयोर्द्वयोः ।\nक्षयं जगाम सा रात्रिर्लोमशं चाविशद्भयम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"While the two spoke thus, both in distress, the night passed, and fear entered Lomasha."}},{"n":109,"text":"ततः प्रभातसमये विकृतः कृष्णपिङ्गलः ।\nस्थूलस्फिग्विकचो रूक्षः श्वचक्रपरिवारितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then at dawn there appeared a Chandala named Parigha, misshapen, dark and tawny, with heavy hips, wide-jawed, rough, surrounded by a pack of dogs,"}},{"n":110,"text":"शङ्कुकर्णो महावक्त्रः पलितो घोरदर्शनः ।\nपरिघो नाम चण्डालः शस्त्रपाणिरदृश्यत ॥","meaning":{"en":"with stake-like ears, a big mouth, gray-haired, terrible to see, weapon in hand."}},{"n":111,"text":"तं दृष्ट्वा यमदूताभं मार्जारस्त्रस्तचेतनः ।\nउवाच पलितं भीतः किमिदानीं करिष्यसि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing him, like a messenger of Yama, the cat, his mind terrified, said fearfully to Palita, 'What will you do now?'"}},{"n":112,"text":"अथ चापि सुसंत्रस्तौ तं दृष्ट्वा घोरदर्शनम् ।\nक्षणेन नकुलोलूकौ नैराश्यं जग्मतुस्तदा ॥","meaning":{"en":"And the mongoose and the owl too, greatly frightened at seeing that terrible sight, in a moment lost hope."}},{"n":113,"text":"बलिनौ मतिमन्तौ च संघातं चाप्युपागतौ ।\nअशक्यौ सुनयात्तस्मात्संप्रधर्षयितुं बलात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Both strong and intelligent, and now joined together, they could not be overpowered by force, and so not by good policy either."}},{"n":114,"text":"कार्यार्थं कृतसंधी तौ दृष्ट्वा मार्जारमूषकौ ।\nउलूकनकुलौ तूर्णं जग्मतुः स्वं स्वमालयम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing the cat and the mouse allied for their purpose, the owl and the mongoose quickly went each to his own home."}},{"n":115,"text":"ततश्चिच्छेद तं तन्तुं मार्जारस्य स मूषकः ।\nविप्रमुक्तोऽथ मार्जारस्तमेवाभ्यपतद्द्रुमम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the mouse cut that thread of the cat's. Freed, the cat leaped up that same tree."}},{"n":116,"text":"स च तस्माद्भयान्मुक्तो मुक्तो घोरेण शत्रुणा ।\nबिलं विवेश पलितः शाखां भेजे च लोमशः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Freed from that fear and from the dreadful enemy, Palita entered his burrow and Lomasha took to the branch."}},{"n":117,"text":"उन्माथमप्यथादाय चण्डालो वीक्ष्य सर्वशः ।\nविहताशः क्षणेनाथ तस्माद्देशादपाक्रमत् ।\nजगाम च स्वभवनं चण्डालो भरतर्षभ ॥","meaning":{"en":"The Chandala took up his snare, looked all about, his hope gone, and in a moment left the place and went to his home, best of the Bharatas."}},{"n":118,"text":"ततस्तस्माद्भयान्मुक्तो दुर्लभं प्राप्य जीवितम् ।\nबिलस्थं पादपाग्रस्थः पलितं लोमशोऽब्रवीत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, freed from that fear, having gained the hard-won gift of life, Lomasha on the treetop said to Palita in his burrow:"}},{"n":119,"text":"अकृत्वा संविदं कांचित्सहसाहमुपप्लुतः ।\nकृतज्ञं कृतकल्याणं कच्चिन्मां नाभिशङ्कसे ॥","meaning":{"en":"'I rushed up without making any agreement. Do you not suspect me, who am grateful and have done good?"}},{"n":120,"text":"गत्वा च मम विश्वासं दत्त्वा च मम जीवितम् ।\nमित्रोपभोगसमये किं त्वं नैवोपसर्पसि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having gone and given me your trust and my life, why do you not come near at the time of enjoying a friend?"}},{"n":121,"text":"कृत्वा हि पूर्वं मित्राणि यः पश्चान्नानुतिष्ठति ।\nन स मित्राणि लभते कृच्छ्रास्वापत्सु दुर्मतिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"One who, having first made friends, does not afterward do his part, that ill-minded man finds no friends in hard calamities."}},{"n":122,"text":"तत्कृतोऽहं त्वया मित्रं सामर्थ्यादात्मनः सखे ।\nस मां मित्रत्वमापन्नमुपभोक्तुं त्वमर्हसि ॥","meaning":{"en":"So by you I was made a friend, through your own power, friend; having become a friend, you should enjoy me."}},{"n":123,"text":"यानि मे सन्ति मित्राणि ये च मे सन्ति बान्धवाः ।\nसर्वे त्वां पूजयिष्यन्ति शिष्या गुरुमिव प्रियम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"All my friends and all my kinsmen will honor you like a dear teacher, as disciples do."}},{"n":124,"text":"अहं च पूजयिष्ये त्वां समित्रगणबान्धवम् ।\nजीवितस्य प्रदातारं कृतज्ञः को न पूजयेत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"And I will honor you with your friends and kin. Who that is grateful would not honor the giver of life?"}},{"n":125,"text":"ईश्वरो मे भवानस्तु शरीरस्य गृहस्य च ।\nअर्थानां चैव सर्वेषामनुशास्ता च मे भव ॥","meaning":{"en":"Be the lord of my body and my house, and be the instructor of all my affairs."}},{"n":126,"text":"अमात्यो मे भव प्राज्ञ पितेव हि प्रशाधि माम् ।\nन तेऽस्ति भयमस्मत्तो जीवितेनात्मनः शपे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Be my minister, wise one, and govern me like a father. I swear by my life that you have no fear from me."}},{"n":127,"text":"बुद्ध्या त्वमुशनाः साक्षाद्बले त्वधिकृता वयम् ।\nत्वन्मन्त्रबलयुक्तो हि विन्देत जयमेव ह ॥","meaning":{"en":"In intelligence you are Ushanas himself; in strength I am the one set over it. Equipped with your counsel and my strength, one would surely win.'"}},{"n":128,"text":"एवमुक्तः परं सान्त्वं मार्जारेण स मूषकः ।\nउवाच परमार्थज्ञः श्लक्ष्णमात्महितं वचः ॥","meaning":{"en":"So addressed with great conciliation by the cat, the mouse, knowing the supreme good, spoke a smooth word for his own benefit."}},{"n":129,"text":"यद्भवानाह तत्सर्वं मया ते लोमश श्रुतम् ।\nममापि तावद्ब्रुवतः शृणु यत्प्रतिभाति माम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"'Lomasha, I have heard all that you said. Now hear what seems right to me as I speak."}},{"n":130,"text":"वेदितव्यानि मित्राणि बोद्धव्याश्चापि शत्रवः ।\nएतत्सुसूक्ष्मं लोकेऽस्मिन्दृश्यते प्राज्ञसंमतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Friends must be known and enemies understood; this is very subtle, and in this world is seen as approved by the wise."}},{"n":131,"text":"शत्रुरूपाश्च सुहृदो मित्ररूपाश्च शत्रवः ।\nसान्त्वितास्ते न बुध्यन्ते रागलोभवशं गताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Friends wear the form of enemies and enemies the form of friends; even when soothed, they do not notice, having come under attachment and greed."}},{"n":132,"text":"नास्ति जात्या रिपुर्नाम मित्रं नाम न विद्यते ।\nसामर्थ्ययोगाज्जायन्ते मित्राणि रिपवस्तथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"By birth there is no such thing as an enemy, and no friend either. Friends and enemies arise through the working of power."}},{"n":133,"text":"यो यस्मिञ्जीवति स्वार्थं पश्येत्तावत्स जीवति ।\nस तस्य तावन्मित्रं स्याद्यावन्न स्याद्विपर्ययः ॥","meaning":{"en":"One who sees his own interest in another's living lives as long as that lasts; he is that man's friend as long as the situation does not reverse."}},{"n":134,"text":"नास्ति मैत्री स्थिरा नाम न च ध्रुवमसौहृदम् ।\nअर्थयुक्त्या हि जायन्ते मित्राणि रिपवस्तथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"There is no friendship that is fixed, and no ill-will that is certain; friends and enemies arise through connection of interests."}},{"n":135,"text":"मित्रं च शत्रुतामेति कस्मिंश्चित्कालपर्यये ।\nशत्रुश्च मित्रतामेति स्वार्थो हि बलवत्तरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"A friend becomes an enemy in some turn of time, and an enemy becomes a friend, for self-interest is the stronger."}},{"n":136,"text":"यो विश्वसति मित्रेषु न चाश्वसति शत्रुषु ।\nअर्थयुक्तिमविज्ञाय चलितं तस्य जीवितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"One who trusts friends and does not trust enemies, without understanding the connection of interests, has his life shaken."}},{"n":137,"text":"अर्थयुक्तिमविज्ञाय यः शुभे कुरुते मतिम् ।\nमित्रे वा यदि वा शत्रौ तस्यापि चलिता मतिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"One who, without understanding the connection of interests, sets his mind on good, whether in a friend or an enemy, has a wavering mind."}},{"n":138,"text":"न विश्वसेदविश्वस्ते विश्वस्तेऽपि न विश्वसेत् ।\nविश्वासाद्भयमुत्पन्नं मूलान्यपि निकृन्तति ॥","meaning":{"en":"One should not trust the untrustworthy, and should not even trust the trusted. Fear born of trust cuts even the roots."}},{"n":139,"text":"अर्थयुक्त्या हि दृश्यन्ते पिता माता सुतास्तथा ।\nमातुला भागिनेयाश्च तथा संबन्धिबान्धवाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"By the connection of interests are seen father, mother, sons, maternal uncles, nephews, in-laws and kinsmen."}},{"n":140,"text":"पुत्रं हि मातापितरु त्यजतः पतितं प्रियम् ।\nलोको रक्षति चात्मानं पश्य स्वार्थस्य सारताम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Mother and father abandon even a beloved son who has fallen, and the world protects itself; see the essence of self-interest."}},{"n":141,"text":"तं मन्ये निकृतिप्रज्ञं यो मोक्षं प्रत्यनन्तरम् ।\nकृत्यं मृगयसे कर्तुं सुखोपायमसंशयम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"I think you have a deceitful mind, who right after release are looking for something to do, no doubt an easy means of pleasure."}},{"n":142,"text":"अस्मिन्निलय एव त्वं न्यग्रोधादवतारितः ।\nपूर्वं निविष्टमुन्माथं चपलत्वान्न बुद्धवान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"You were brought down from the banyan to this very dwelling, and in your fickleness you did not notice the snare set there earlier."}},{"n":143,"text":"आत्मनश्चपलो नास्ति कुतोऽन्येषां भविष्यति ।\nतस्मात्सर्वाणि कार्याणि चपलो हन्त्यसंशयम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"One fickle toward himself is nothing; how will he be toward others? Therefore a fickle man destroys all his tasks, without doubt."}},{"n":144,"text":"ब्रवीति मधुरं कंचित्प्रियो मे ह भवानिति ।\nतन्मिथ्याकरणं सर्वं विस्तरेणापि मे शृणु ॥","meaning":{"en":"Someone says sweetly, 'You are dear to me.' Hear in full how all that is false."}},{"n":145,"text":"कारणात्प्रियतामेति द्वेष्यो भवति कारणात् ।\nअर्थार्थी जीवलोकोऽयं न कश्चित्कस्यचित्प्रियः ॥","meaning":{"en":"By a reason one becomes dear and by a reason one becomes hated. This living world is bent on gain; no one is dear to anyone."}},{"n":146,"text":"सख्यं सोदरयोर्भ्रात्रोर्दंपत्योर्वा परस्परम् ।\nकस्यचिन्नाभिजानामि प्रीतिं निष्कारणामिह ॥","meaning":{"en":"Friendship between brothers of the same womb or between husband and wife: I know of no one's affection here without a cause."}},{"n":147,"text":"यद्यपि भ्रातरः क्रुद्धा भार्या वा कारणान्तरे ।\nस्वभावतस्ते प्रीयन्ते नेतरः प्रीयते जनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Even angry brothers or a wife may, for another reason, be pleased by nature; no other person is pleased so."}},{"n":148,"text":"प्रियो भवति दानेन प्रियवादेन चापरः ।\nमन्त्रहोमजपैरन्यः कार्यार्थं प्रीयते जनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"One becomes dear by gifts, another by sweet speech, another by mantras, oblations and prayers; people are pleased for the sake of an aim."}},{"n":149,"text":"उत्पन्ने कारणे प्रीतिर्नास्ति नौ कारणान्तरे ।\nप्रध्वस्ते कारणस्थाने सा प्रीतिर्विनिवर्तते ॥","meaning":{"en":"When a reason arises there is affection; when the reason is gone, that affection turns back; and so between us."}},{"n":150,"text":"किं नु तत्कारणं मन्ये येनाहं भवतः प्रियः ।\nअन्यत्राभ्यवहारार्थात्तत्रापि च बुधा वयम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"What reason do I suppose there is for which I am dear to you, apart from the purpose of eating? And in that I am wise."}},{"n":151,"text":"कालो हेतुं विकुरुते स्वार्थस्तमनुवर्तते ।\nस्वार्थं प्राज्ञोऽभिजानाति प्राज्ञं लोकोऽनुवर्तते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Time changes the cause, and self-interest follows it. The wise man knows his own interest, and the world follows the wise."}},{"n":152,"text":"न त्वीदृशं त्वया वाच्यं विदुषि स्वार्थपण्डिते ।\nअकालेऽविषमस्थस्य स्वार्थहेतुरयं तव ॥","meaning":{"en":"You should not speak like this to one who is learned and expert in his own interest; you do so at the wrong time, for one not in distress, for the sake of your own interest."}},{"n":153,"text":"तस्मान्नाहं चले स्वार्थात्सुस्थितः संधिविग्रहे ।\nअभ्राणामिव रूपाणि विकुर्वन्ति क्षणे क्षणे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Therefore I do not waver from my interest, being well settled in peace and war. Clouds change their forms every moment."}},{"n":154,"text":"अद्यैव हि रिपुर्भूत्वा पुनरद्यैव सौहृदम् ।\nपुनश्च रिपुरद्यैव युक्तीनां पश्य चापलम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Today one becomes an enemy and again today a friend, and again today an enemy; see the fickleness of arrangements."}},{"n":155,"text":"आसीत्तावत्तु मैत्री नौ यावद्धेतुरभूत्पुरा ।\nसा गता सह तेनैव कालयुक्तेन हेतुना ॥","meaning":{"en":"Our friendship lasted only as long as the cause existed before; it has gone with that very cause, tied to its time."}},{"n":156,"text":"त्वं हि मेऽत्यन्ततः शत्रुः सामर्थ्यान्मित्रतां गतः ।\nतत्कृत्यमभिनिर्वृत्तं प्रकृतिः शत्रुतां गता ॥","meaning":{"en":"You are my utter enemy; you became a friend by force of circumstance. That task is done, and your nature has gone back to enmity."}},{"n":157,"text":"सोऽहमेवं प्रणीतानि ज्ञात्वा शास्त्राणि तत्त्वतः ।\nप्रविशेयं कथं पाशं त्वत्कृतं तद्वदस्व मे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Knowing the scriptures thus truthfully laid down, how should I walk into a snare of your making? Tell me."}},{"n":158,"text":"त्वद्वीर्येण विमुक्तोऽहं मद्वीर्येण तथा भवान् ।\nअन्योन्यानुग्रहे वृत्ते नास्ति भूयः समागमः ॥","meaning":{"en":"I was released by your strength and you by mine; with mutual help done, there is no further meeting."}},{"n":159,"text":"त्वं हि सौम्य कृतार्थोऽद्य निर्वृत्तार्थास्तथा वयम् ।\nन तेऽस्त्यन्यन्मया कृत्यं किंचिदन्यत्र भक्षणात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"You, gentle one, have your aim accomplished today and so have I. You have nothing else to do with me except eating me."}},{"n":160,"text":"अहमन्नं भवान्भोक्ता दुर्बलोऽहं भवान्बली ।\nनावयोर्विद्यते संधिर्नियुक्ते विषमे बले ॥","meaning":{"en":"I am food and you are the eater; I am weak and you are strong. Between us there is no alliance, when strength is unequal and bent on this."}},{"n":161,"text":"संमन्येऽहं तव प्रज्ञां यन्मोक्षात्प्रत्यनन्तरम् ।\nभक्ष्यं मृगयसे नूनं सुखोपायमसंशयम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"I admire your cleverness, that right after your release you look for food, surely an easy means of pleasure."}},{"n":162,"text":"भक्ष्यार्थमेव बद्धस्त्वं स मुक्तः प्रसृतः क्षुधा ।\nशास्त्रज्ञमभिसंधाय नूनं भक्षयिताद्य माम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"You were bound only for food; freed, you have gone out in hunger. Surely, having secured one who knows the scriptures, you will eat me today."}},{"n":163,"text":"जानामि क्षुधितं हि त्वामाहारसमयश्च ते ।\nस त्वं मामभिसंधाय भक्ष्यं मृगयसे पुनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"I know that you are hungry and that it is your mealtime; you intend me, and again look for prey."}},{"n":164,"text":"यच्चापि पुत्रदारं स्वं तत्संनिसृजसे मयि ।\nशुश्रूषां नाम मे कर्तुं सखे मम न तत्क्षमम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"And as for your sons and wife whom you hand over to me, friend, serving them is not suitable for me."}},{"n":165,"text":"त्वया मां सहितं दृष्ट्वा प्रिया भार्या सुताश्च ये ।\nकस्मान्मां ते न खादेयुर्हृष्टाः प्रणयिनस्त्वयि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing me with you, why would your dear wife and sons, happy and fond of you, not eat me?"}},{"n":166,"text":"नाहं त्वया समेष्यामि वृत्तो हेतुः समागमे ।\nशिवं ध्यायस्व मेऽत्रस्थः सुकृतं स्मर्यते यदि ॥","meaning":{"en":"I will not meet you; the reason for our meeting is past. Meditate on my welfare from where you are, if a good deed is remembered."}},{"n":167,"text":"शत्रोरन्नाद्यभूतः सन्क्लिष्टस्य क्षुधितस्य च ।\nभक्ष्यं मृगयमाणस्य कः प्राज्ञो विषयं व्रजेत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Who wise would go into the grasp of an enemy who is troubled and hungry, looking for prey, becoming his food?"}},{"n":168,"text":"स्वस्ति तेऽस्तु गमिष्यामि दूरादपि तवोद्विजे ।\nनाहं त्वया समेष्यामि निर्वृतो भव लोमश ॥","meaning":{"en":"May you be safe; I will go; even from afar I am afraid of you. I will not meet you; be at ease, Lomasha."}},{"n":169,"text":"बलवत्संनिकर्षो हि न कदाचित्प्रशस्यते ।\nप्रशान्तादपि मे प्राज्ञ भेतव्यं बलिनः सदा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Closeness to the strong is never praised. Even from a calm strong one, wise one, I must always be afraid."}},{"n":170,"text":"यदि त्वर्थेन मे कार्यं ब्रूहि किं करवाणि ते ।\nकामं सर्वं प्रदास्यामि न त्वात्मानं कदाचन ॥","meaning":{"en":"But if you need something from me, say what I can do for you. I will gladly give everything, but never myself."}},{"n":171,"text":"आत्मार्थे संततिस्त्याज्या राज्यं रत्नं धनं तथा ।\nअपि सर्वस्वमुत्सृज्य रक्षेदात्मानमात्मना ॥","meaning":{"en":"For one's own self one should give up offspring, kingdom, jewels and wealth. Even giving up all one has, one should guard oneself by oneself."}},{"n":172,"text":"ऐश्वर्यधनरत्नानां प्रत्यमित्रेऽपि तिष्ठताम् ।\nदृष्टा हि पुनरावृत्तिर्जीवतामिति नः श्रुतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"For those who keep sovereignty, wealth and jewels, even against an enemy, we have heard that return is seen while they live."}},{"n":173,"text":"न त्वात्मनः संप्रदानं धनरत्नवदिष्यते ।\nआत्मा तु सर्वतो रक्ष्यो दारैरपि धनैरपि ॥","meaning":{"en":"But giving up oneself is not approved like wealth and jewels. One's self should be guarded in every way, even at the cost of wives and riches."}},{"n":174,"text":"आत्मरक्षिततन्त्राणां सुपरीक्षितकारिणाम् ।\nआपदो नोपपद्यन्ते पुरुषाणां स्वदोषजाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"For men who guard themselves and act after careful examination, calamities born of their own faults do not arise."}},{"n":175,"text":"शत्रून्सम्यग्विजानन्ति दुर्बला ये बलीयसः ।\nतेषां न चाल्यते बुद्धिरात्मार्थं कृतनिश्चया ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those weak ones who rightly understand stronger enemies do not have their minds shaken, being resolved for their own good.'"}},{"n":176,"text":"इत्यभिव्यक्तमेवासौ पलितेनावभर्त्सितः ।\nमार्जारो व्रीडितो भूत्वा मूषकं वाक्यमब्रवीत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Thus plainly rebuked by Palita, the cat, ashamed, said to the mouse:"}},{"n":177,"text":"संमन्येऽहं तव प्रज्ञां यस्त्वं मम हिते रतः ।\nउक्तवानर्थतत्त्वेन मया संभिन्नदर्शनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"'I admire your wisdom, that you are intent on my good; you spoke the truth of the matter while I had a divided view."}},{"n":178,"text":"न तु मामन्यथा साधो त्वं विज्ञातुमिहार्हसि ।\nप्राणप्रदानजं त्वत्तो मम सौहृदमागतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"But you should not understand me otherwise, good one; friendship with you has come to me from your giving me life."}},{"n":179,"text":"धर्मज्ञोऽस्मि गुणज्ञोऽस्मि कृतज्ञोऽस्मि विशेषतः ।\nमित्रेषु वत्सलश्चास्मि त्वद्विधेषु विशेषतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"I know dharma, I know virtue, and above all I am grateful. I am affectionate toward friends, especially those like you."}},{"n":180,"text":"तन्मामेवंगते साधो न यावयितुमर्हसि ।\nत्वया हि याव्यमानोऽहं प्राणाञ्जह्यां सबान्धवः ॥","meaning":{"en":"So, being in this state, good one, you should not drive me off. If driven off by you, I would give up my life with my kin."}},{"n":181,"text":"धिक्शब्दो हि बुधैर्दृष्टो मद्विधेषु मनस्विषु ।\nमरणं धर्मतत्त्वज्ञ न मां शङ्कितुमर्हसि ॥","meaning":{"en":"The wise see the word 'shame' applied to high-minded ones like me. I would rather die; you should not suspect me, knower of dharma's truth.'"}},{"n":182,"text":"इति संस्तूयमानो हि मार्जारेण स मूषकः ।\nमनसा भावगम्भीरं मार्जारं वाक्यमब्रवीत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"So praised by the cat, the mouse in his mind, deep in feeling, said to the cat:"}},{"n":183,"text":"साधुर्भवाञ्श्रुतार्थोऽस्मि प्रीयते न च विश्वसे ।\nसंस्तवैर्वा धनौघैर्वा नाहं शक्यः पुनस्त्वया ॥","meaning":{"en":"'You are good, and I have heard your meaning and am pleased, but I do not trust. By praises or floods of wealth you cannot win me again."}},{"n":184,"text":"न ह्यमित्रवशं यान्ति प्राज्ञा निष्कारणं सखे ।\nअस्मिन्नर्थे च गाथे द्वे निबोधोशनसा कृते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Wise ones do not go into an enemy's power without cause, friend. On this matter hear two verses made by Ushanas."}},{"n":185,"text":"शत्रुसाधारणे कृत्ये कृत्वा संधिं बलीयसा ।\nसमाहितश्चरेद्युक्त्या कृतार्थश्च न विश्वसेत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"In a task shared against an enemy, having made peace with a stronger one, one should proceed carefully and wisely, and, his purpose achieved, should not trust."}},{"n":186,"text":"तस्मात्सर्वास्ववस्थासु रक्षेज्जीवितमात्मनः ।\nद्रव्याणि संततिश्चैव सर्वं भवति जीवतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Therefore in all circumstances one should protect one's own life; wealth and offspring and everything belong to one who lives."}},{"n":187,"text":"संक्षेपो नीतिशास्त्राणामविश्वासः परो मतः ।\nनृषु तस्मादविश्वासः पुष्कलं हितमात्मनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The summary of the treatises on policy is held to be distrust above all. Therefore distrust among men is ample benefit for oneself."}},{"n":188,"text":"वध्यन्ते न ह्यविश्वस्ताः शत्रुभिर्दुर्बला अपि ।\nविश्वस्तास्त्वाशु वध्यन्ते बलवन्तोऽपि दुर्बलैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those who do not trust are not killed by enemies, even weak ones; but those who trust are quickly killed by the weak, even if they are strong."}},{"n":189,"text":"त्वद्विधेभ्यो मया ह्यात्मा रक्ष्यो मार्जार सर्वदा ।\nरक्ष त्वमपि चात्मानं चण्डालाज्जातिकिल्बिषात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"I must always protect myself from the likes of you, cat. You too protect yourself from the Chandala, the blemish of his birth.'"}},{"n":190,"text":"स तस्य ब्रुवतस्त्वेवं संत्रासाज्जातसाध्वसः ।\nस्वबिलं हि जवेनाशु मार्जारः प्रययौ ततः ॥","meaning":{"en":"While he spoke, the cat, seized by terror, quickly ran off at speed to his own place."}},{"n":191,"text":"ततः शास्त्रार्थतत्त्वज्ञो बुद्धिसामर्थ्यमात्मनः ।\nविश्राव्य पलितः प्राज्ञो बिलमन्यज्जगाम ह ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the wise Palita, knower of the truth of the scriptures, having displayed his own intelligence and ability, went to another burrow."}},{"n":192,"text":"एवं प्रज्ञावता बुद्ध्या दुर्बलेन महाबलाः ।\nएकेन बहवोऽमित्राः पलितेनाभिसंधिताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Thus by a wise mind, a weak one, Palita alone, outwitted many great and strong enemies."}},{"n":193,"text":"अरिणापि समर्थेन संधिं कुर्वीत पण्डितः ।\nमूषकश्च बिडालश्च मुक्तावन्योन्यसंश्रयात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The wise man should make peace even with a capable enemy; the mouse and the cat were freed by relying on each other."}},{"n":194,"text":"इत्येष क्षत्रधर्मस्य मया मार्गोऽनुदर्शितः ।\nविस्तरेण महीपाल संक्षेपेण पुनः शृणु ॥","meaning":{"en":"This is the path of the warrior's duty that I have shown you at length, king; hear it now in brief."}},{"n":195,"text":"अन्योन्यकृतवैरौ तु चक्रतुः प्रीतिमुत्तमाम् ।\nअन्योन्यमभिसंधातुमभूच्चैव तयोर्मतिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Though they had made enmity with each other, they made excellent friendship, and each had it in mind to outwit the other."}},{"n":196,"text":"तत्र प्राज्ञोऽभिसंधत्ते सम्यग्बुद्धिबलाश्रयात् ।\nअभिसंधीयते प्राज्ञः प्रमादादपि चाबुधैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"There the wise one outwits by relying on the strength of his mind well used, and the wise one is outwitted by fools through his own carelessness."}},{"n":197,"text":"तस्मादभीतवद्भीतो विश्वस्तवदविश्वसन् ।\nन ह्यप्रमत्तश्चलति चलितो वा विनश्यति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Therefore, fearing like one not afraid, distrusting like one who trusts: for one who is careful does not waver, and one who wavers is destroyed."}},{"n":198,"text":"कालेन रिपुणा संधिः काले मित्रेण विग्रहः ।\nकार्य इत्येव तत्त्वज्ञाः प्राहुर्नित्यं युधिष्ठिर ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those who know the truth always say, Yudhishthira, that one should make peace with an enemy in due time and make war with a friend in due time."}},{"n":199,"text":"एवं मत्वा महाराज शास्त्रार्थमभिगम्य च ।\nअभियुक्तोऽप्रमत्तश्च प्राग्भयाद्भीतवच्चरेत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Thinking so, great king, and having mastered the meaning of the scriptures, one should be diligent and careful and act as if afraid even before fear comes."}},{"n":200,"text":"भीतवत्संविधिः कार्यः प्रतिसंधिस्तथैव च ।\nभयादुत्पद्यते बुद्धिरप्रमत्ताभियोगजा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Arrangements and counter-arrangements should be made as if afraid; from fear arises the thought that comes from careful effort."}},{"n":201,"text":"न भयं विद्यते राजन्भीतस्यानागते भये ।\nअभीतस्य तु विस्रम्भात्सुमहज्जायते भयम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"King, one who is afraid has no fear when fear is yet to come, but great fear arises for one who is fearless from trust."}},{"n":202,"text":"न भीरुरिति चात्यन्तं मन्त्रोऽदेयः कथंचन ।\nअविज्ञानाद्धि विज्ञाते गच्छेदास्पददर्शिषु ॥","meaning":{"en":"One should never give counsel to a man simply because he is 'not timid'; through ignorance it may go to those who look for a foothold in what they know."}},{"n":203,"text":"तस्मादभीतवद्भीतो विश्वस्तवदविश्वसन् ।\nकार्याणां गुरुतां बुद्ध्वा नानृतं किंचिदाचरेत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Therefore, fearing like one not afraid and distrusting like one who trusts, realizing the weight of affairs, one should do nothing false."}},{"n":204,"text":"एवमेतन्मया प्रोक्तमितिहासं युधिष्ठिर ।\nश्रुत्वा त्वं सुहृदां मध्ये यथावत्समुपाचर ॥","meaning":{"en":"Yudhishthira, I have told you this tale; having heard it, act properly among your friends."}},{"n":205,"text":"उपलभ्य मतिं चाग्र्यामरिमित्रान्तरं तथा ।\nसंधिविग्रहकालं च मोक्षोपायं तथापदि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having grasped the best intelligence, the difference between enemy and friend, the time for peace and war, and the means of escape in calamity,"}},{"n":206,"text":"शत्रुसाधारणे कृत्ये कृत्वा संधिं बलीयसा ।\nसमागमं चरेद्युक्त्या कृतार्थो न च विश्वसेत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"in a task shared against an enemy, having made peace with a stronger one, meet with wisdom, and when your aim is achieved, do not trust."}},{"n":207,"text":"अविरुद्धां त्रिवर्गेण नीतिमेतां युधिष्ठिर ।\nअभ्युत्तिष्ठ श्रुतादस्माद्भूयस्त्वं रञ्जयन्प्रजाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Yudhishthira, this policy is consistent with the three aims of life. Rise up after hearing it, and again please your people."}},{"n":208,"text":"ब्राह्मणैश्चापि ते सार्धं यात्रा भवतु पाण्डव ।\nब्राह्मणा हि परं श्रेयो दिवि चेह च भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"And let your journey, Pandava, be together with brahmins, for brahmins are the highest good, in heaven and here, Bharata."}},{"n":209,"text":"एते धर्मस्य वेत्तारः कृतज्ञाः सततं प्रभो ।\nपूजिताः शुभकर्माणः पूर्वजित्या नराधिप ॥","meaning":{"en":"These are knowers of dharma and ever grateful, lord. Honored, they do good deeds; so, lord of men, by the former conquest."}},{"n":210,"text":"राज्यं श्रेयः परं राजन्यशः कीर्तिं च लप्स्यसे ।\nकुलस्य संततिं चैव यथान्यायं यथाक्रमम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"King, you will gain the highest welfare in your kingdom, fame and renown, and the continuation of your family, rightly and in order."}},{"n":211,"text":"द्वयोरिमं भारत संधिविग्रहं\nसुभाषितं बुद्धिविशेषकारितम् ।\nतथान्ववेक्ष्य क्षितिपेन सर्वदा\nनिषेवितव्यं नृप शत्रुमण्डले ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bharata, this well-spoken account of peace and war between two, produced by superior intelligence, should be considered and always practiced by a king, O king, against a circle of enemies."}}]}]}